    "turn_text": "I'll tell you what the exact right amount is today, $14. How do I know that? We analyzed it. As I told somebody who was walking with me today, I'm a great Napoleonic fan, where he once said, don't tell my wife, make sure she doesn't see this. If I were to be in love, I'd analyze it bit by bit because you can't ask how or why enough. So what we did when I lost, I didn't go for a lobbying job like 150 congressmen and senators. I went to teach and work on nonprofits. And as we teach, we analyze what's the right minimum wage. So we studied all those cool terminus counties. Like in New Jersey, they raised the minimum wage. And we looked at the counties over here that didn't in Pennsylvania. We found out that they did not as well as scores and scores of others lose any jobs as long as you didn't raise it above the average hourly wage. So you could go up to $14 today. which is the average hourly weight, and you don't lose a job. Above that, you begin to lose it. So that's why I just said, let's analyze it, look at it, and show by fax, who does fax today.",
